        system_tag: 'Neurology',
        difficulty: 'medium',
        explanation: `This presentation — ascending, symmetric weakness with areflexia following a preceding gastrointestinal (classically Campylobacter jejuni) or respiratory infection, with albuminocytologic dissociation (elevated CSF protein without pleocytosis) — is Guillain-Barré syndrome. It results from molecular mimicry: antibodies generated against microbial antigens cross-react with peripheral nerve gangliosides/myelin, producing an autoimmune, predominantly demyelinating polyradiculoneuropathy.`,
