        stem: `A 22-year-old woman with a history of recurrent sinus infections and two prior unexplained episodes of giardiasis receives a unit of fresh frozen plasma for a coagulopathy. Within minutes of starting the infusion she develops severe dyspnea, diffuse wheezing, and hypotension, without fever or chills. The infusion is stopped immediately and she is treated with epinephrine and supportive care. Subsequent workup shows a negative direct antiglobulin (Coombs) test and a normal serum haptoglobin.`,
