        stem: `A 68-year-old woman with a mechanical mitral valve on stable long-term warfarin therapy (INR consistently 2.5-3.0) is started on trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole for a urinary tract infection. Ten days later, she presents with gum bleeding and hematuria. Her INR is now 8.2, and no warfarin dose change was made.`,
